{%- comment -%}
  Craftsmanship storytelling — multiple sequential material/process chapters (Design & form,
  Stone setting, Gold & finishing, Quality review, Hallmark, Care…). Used on the homepage, the
  dedicated Craftsmanship page, and (as "House pillars", unrelated content) The House page.
  Material truth only — no unsupported artisan/origin claims.

  Because this one section is shared across three different content contexts, the two settings
  that change its whole composition — `color_scheme` and `layout` — both default to the values
  those existing pages already rely on implicitly ('bone' background, the per-chapter-row list),
  so adding them here changes nothing for page.craftsmanship.json or page.house.json unless a
  merchant explicitly opts in. Only the homepage instance (templates/index.json) sets
  layout: "dominant_image" and color_scheme: "obsidian" explicitly.

  layout: "list" (default, unchanged) — each imaged chapter keeps its own balanced media-and-text
    row; with no images at all, chapters become a balanced multi-column staggered text layout
    (never a permanently blank image column).
  layout: "dominant_image" (new) — one large visual (the new dedicated main_image, or else a
    controlled CAVIERA material field when none is set — never a simulated photo) beside a
    vertical editorial list of the same chapters. A chapter's own per-block image (if any) is not
    additionally shown in this layout, to avoid competing imagery beside an already-dominant visual.
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign layout = section.settings.layout | default: 'list'

  assign any_chapter_has_image = false
  assign any_chapter_has_title = false
  for block in section.blocks
    if block.settings.image != blank
      assign any_chapter_has_image = true
    endif
    if block.settings.title != blank
      assign any_chapter_has_title = true
    endif
  endfor
  assign has_content = any_chapter_has_title
  if section.settings.eyebrow != blank or section.settings.heading != blank or section.settings.intro != blank
    assign has_content = true
  endif

  assign mark_mode = 'light'
  unless section.settings.color_scheme == 'bone'
    assign mark_mode = 'dark'
  endunless

  assign main_image = section.settings.main_image
  assign main_image_mobile = section.settings.main_image_mobile | default: main_image
  assign has_main_image = false
  if main_image != blank
    assign has_main_image = true
  endif
-%}
{%- if has_content -%}
<section class="caviera-section caviera-craftsmanship" data-scheme="{{ section.settings.color_scheme | default: 'bone' }}">
  {%- comment -%}
    Scroll progression — opt-in (see scroll_progression below), off by default since this same
    section renders on the dedicated Craftsmanship page and The House page too, where a scroll-
    driven chapter progression wasn't asked for. templates/index.json turns it on explicitly for
    the homepage ("Material Truth") instance only. .caviera-craftsmanship__stage is the ONLY
    element that gets the extra height (desktop only, see caviera-home.css) — kept as a child div,
    not the outer <section>, so the closing hallmark mark below (if enabled) is never clipped by a
    fixed-height ancestor. Independent of every other section's own scroll system: --material-
    progress and data-material-state here, never --caviera-progress, --house-code-progress, or
    --edition-exhibition-progress.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="caviera-craftsmanship__stage"{% if section.settings.scroll_progression %} data-caviera-material-progress{% endif %}>
    {%- comment -%}
      Continuous looping craftsmanship footage — a separate, independent visual layer BEHIND the
      existing chapter content, never wired to Material Truth's own scroll-progress controller
      (assets/caviera-material-truth.js, untouched). Gated on the same scroll_progression flag as
      the rest of this homepage-only ceremony (this section is shared with the standalone
      Craftsmanship page and The House page too, where this footage/overlay treatment wasn't
      asked for and would fight their own bone/list compositions) — no separate schema setting
      needed since this flag already, correctly, identifies only this one instance.
      assets/caviera-craftsmanship-process-video.js is a small, independent IntersectionObserver-
      based play/pause controller — plain HTML5 video playback, no scroll listener, no RAF loop, no
      interaction whatsoever with Material Truth's or Maker's Mark's own controllers.

      DELIVERY ASSET: the approved source file itself (caviera-material-truth-full-process-
      2026.mp4, kept exactly as supplied — never renamed, moved or re-encoded) is 48MB, over
      Shopify's theme-asset upload limit (confirmed directly — a push attempt failed outright with
      HTTP 413). caviera-material-truth-full-process-2026-optimized.mp4 is a same-footage, re-
      encoded copy (720x1280, ~11.3MB) created only because the original could not technically be
      uploaded at all — this is the file actually referenced below. The original source asset is
      untouched and still present in assets/ exactly as provided.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if section.settings.scroll_progression -%}
      <div class="caviera-craftsmanship__process-video" data-craftsmanship-process-video aria-hidden="true">
        <video class="caviera-craftsmanship__process-video-el" muted loop playsinline preload="none">
          <source src="{{ 'caviera-material-truth-full-process-2026-optimized.mp4' | asset_url }}" type="video/mp4">
        </video>
        <div class="caviera-craftsmanship__process-overlay"></div>
      </div>
      <script src="{{ 'caviera-craftsmanship-process-video.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>
    {%- endif -%}
    <div class="caviera-craftsmanship__stage-inner">
      <div class="container caviera-craftsmanship__head" data-reveal>
        {%- if section.settings.eyebrow != blank -%}<span class="eyebrow">{{ section.settings.eyebrow }}</span>{%- endif -%}
        {%- if section.settings.heading != blank -%}
          {%- comment -%}
            Drkst-style typographic moment, opt-in per instance (see heading_motion below) — off by
            default since this same section renders on the dedicated Craftsmanship page and The
            House page too, where a chapter-moment entrance wasn't asked for. templates/index.json
            turns it on explicitly for the homepage instance only. When scroll_progression is ALSO
            on, this same heading additionally drifts a couple of vw horizontally in step with
            --material-progress for as long as the stage holds (see caviera-home.css) — a
            continuous architectural cue layered on top of its existing one-shot entrance, not a
            replacement for it.
          {%- endcomment -%}
          <h2 class="heading-h2"{% if section.settings.heading_motion %} data-reveal data-reveal-style="drkst"{% endif %}>{{ section.settings.heading }}</h2>
        {%- endif -%}
        {%- if section.settings.intro != blank -%}<div class="body-text--wide">{{ section.settings.intro }}</div>{%- endif -%}
        {%- if section.settings.scroll_progression -%}
          <span class="caviera-craftsmanship__progress" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      {%- if layout == 'dominant_image' -%}
    <div class="container caviera-craftsmanship__split">
      <div class="caviera-craftsmanship__visual-col">
        <div class="caviera-craftsmanship__visual">
          {%- if has_main_image -%}
            <span class="caviera-craftsmanship__visual-offset" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <div class="caviera-craftsmanship__visual-frame">
              <picture>
                {%- if main_image_mobile != blank and main_image_mobile != main_image -%}
                  <source media="(max-width: 749px)" srcset="{{ main_image_mobile | image_url: width: 700 }} 700w, {{ main_image_mobile | image_url: width: 1000 }} 1000w" sizes="100vw">
                {%- endif -%}
                <img
                  src="{{ main_image | image_url: width: 1200 }}"
                  srcset="{{ main_image | image_url: width: 600 }} 600w, {{ main_image | image_url: width: 1200 }} 1200w, {{ main_image | image_url: width: 1800 }} 1800w"
                  sizes="(min-width: 1024px) 52vw, 100vw"
                  width="{{ main_image.width }}" height="{{ main_image.height }}"
                  alt="{{ main_image.alt | default: '' | escape }}"
                  loading="lazy"
                >
              </picture>
            </div>
          {%- else -%}
            {%- comment -%}
              Controlled CAVIERA material field — never a simulated photo. Same "Cinnabar panel,
              Warm Bone inset" language as Object in focus and Packaging ritual's own compositions.
            {%- endcomment -%}
            <div class="caviera-craftsmanship__composition" aria-hidden="true">
              <span class="caviera-craftsmanship__composition-inset"></span>
            </div>
            {%- if section.settings.show_seal_watermark -%}
              <div class="caviera-craftsmanship__composition-seal" style="--seal-opacity: {{ section.settings.seal_watermark_opacity | default: 6 }}%;">
                {%- render 'caviera-house-seal', mode: mark_mode, width: 220, alt: '' -%}
              </div>
            {%- endif -%}
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="caviera-craftsmanship__stories">
        {%- if any_chapter_has_title -%}
          <ol class="caviera-craftsmanship__story-list">
            {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
              {%- if block.settings.title != blank -%}
                <li class="caviera-craftsmanship__story" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
                  <span class="caviera-craftsmanship__story-number label" aria-hidden="true">{% if forloop.index < 10 %}0{% endif %}{{ forloop.index }}</span>
                  <h3 class="caviera-craftsmanship__story-title">{{ block.settings.title }}</h3>
                  {%- if block.settings.body != blank -%}<div class="body-text">{{ block.settings.body }}</div>{%- endif -%}
                </li>
              {%- endif -%}
            {%- endfor -%}
          </ol>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>
    </div>
  {%- else -%}
    {%- if any_chapter_has_title -%}
      <div class="container caviera-craftsmanship__list" data-media="{% if any_chapter_has_image %}yes{% else %}no{% endif %}">
        {%- for block in section.blocks -%}
          {%- if block.settings.title != blank -%}
            <article class="caviera-craftsmanship__row{% if block.settings.image == blank %} caviera-craftsmanship__row--text-only{% endif %}" data-reveal data-chapter-index="{{ forloop.index0 }}" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
              {%- if block.settings.image -%}
                <div class="caviera-craftsmanship__image">
                  <img
                    src="{{ block.settings.image | image_url: width: 800 }}"
                    srcset="{{ block.settings.image | image_url: width: 400 }} 400w, {{ block.settings.image | image_url: width: 800 }} 800w"
                    sizes="(min-width: 900px) 33vw, 100vw"
                    width="{{ block.settings.image.width }}" height="{{ block.settings.image.height }}"
                    alt="{{ block.settings.image.alt | default: '' | escape }}"
                    loading="lazy"
                  >
                </div>
              {%- endif -%}
              <div class="caviera-craftsmanship__copy">
                <span class="label">{% if forloop.index < 10 %}0{% endif %}{{ forloop.index }}</span>
                <h3 class="heading-h3">{{ block.settings.title }}</h3>
                {%- if block.settings.body != blank -%}<div class="body-text">{{ block.settings.body }}</div>{%- endif -%}
              </div>
            </article>
          {%- endif -%}
        {%- endfor -%}
      </div>
    {%- elsif request.design_mode -%}
      <div class="container"><div class="caviera-editor-note">Add up to six chapter blocks (e.g. Design & form, Stone setting, Gold & finishing).</div></div>
    {%- endif -%}
  {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>

  {%- if section.settings.show_hallmark -%}
    <div class="caviera-craftsmanship__hallmark" data-reveal>
      {%- render 'caviera-house-seal', mode: mark_mode, width: 56 -%}
    </div>
  {%- endif -%}
</section>
{%- if section.settings.scroll_progression -%}
  <script src="{{ 'caviera-material-truth.js' | asset_url }}" defer="defer"></script>
{%- endif -%}
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Craftsmanship",
  "settings": [
    { "type": "text", "id": "eyebrow", "label": "Eyebrow", "default": "Craftsmanship" },
    { "type": "text", "id": "heading", "label": "Heading", "default": "Material truth." },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "heading_motion", "label": "Oversized heading entrance", "default": false, "info": "A restrained Drkst-style typographic moment for this heading. Off by default — this section is shared with the Craftsmanship and House pages; the homepage instance turns it on explicitly." },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "scroll_progression", "label": "Scroll-driven chapter progression", "default": false, "info": "A brief, light sticky hold (desktop only, ~50vh of extra scroll) while the chapters activate one at a time and the heading drifts slightly — a restrained Drkst/Rumaya-inspired moment. Off by default — this section is shared with the Craftsmanship and House pages, where this wasn't asked for; the homepage instance turns it on explicitly. Off renders the plain static section exactly as before." },
    { "type": "richtext", "id": "intro", "label": "Intro" },
    {
      "type": "select", "id": "color_scheme", "label": "Colour", "default": "bone",
      "options": [
        { "value": "bone", "label": "Warm Bone" },
        { "value": "cinnabar", "label": "Cinnabar" },
        { "value": "obsidian", "label": "Obsidian" }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "select", "id": "layout", "label": "Layout", "default": "list",
      "info": "\"Editorial list\" is the original per-chapter layout, unchanged. \"Dominant image\" pairs one large visual with the chapters as a vertical list beside it.",
      "options": [
        { "value": "list", "label": "Editorial list (per-chapter images optional)" },
        { "value": "dominant_image", "label": "Dominant image + story list" }
      ]
    },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Dominant image layout" },
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "main_image", "label": "Main image (desktop)", "info": "Macro, material or process photography — sketch/CAD detail, diamond-setting macro, polished gold macro. No marketplace badges or promotional text." },
    { "type": "image_picker", "id": "main_image_mobile", "label": "Main image (mobile)", "info": "Falls back to the desktop image when left blank." },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_seal_watermark", "label": "Show House Seal watermark when no image is set", "default": false, "info": "A large, very quiet House Seal in the material field shown only when no main image is configured — optional, and never shown over real photography." },
    { "type": "range", "id": "seal_watermark_opacity", "label": "Watermark opacity", "min": 4, "max": 8, "step": 1, "default": 6, "unit": "%" },
    { "type": "header", "content": "Closing mark" },
    { "type": "checkbox", "id": "show_hallmark", "label": "Show House Seal as closing hallmark", "default": false }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "chapter",
      "name": "Chapter",
      "settings": [
        { "type": "image_picker", "id": "image", "label": "Image", "info": "Used in \"Editorial list\" layout only." },
        { "type": "text", "id": "title", "label": "Title", "info": "e.g. Design & form, Stone setting, Gold & finishing, Quality review" },
        { "type": "richtext", "id": "body", "label": "Body" }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "max_blocks": 6,
  "presets": [
    { "name": "Craftsmanship", "blocks": [{ "type": "chapter" }, { "type": "chapter" }, { "type": "chapter" }] }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
